# AyMidi for WebCLAP

AyMidi (a MIDI synthesizer emulating the AY-3-8910 and YM2149 sound chips, based on Ayumi), ported to WebCLAP. This is not an official release.

- AyMidi: https://github.com/berarma/aymidi (commit 73d233f, GPL-2.0)
- [DPF](https://github.com/DISTRHO/DPF) (commit 4238e1c), the DISTRHO Plugin Framework the plugin is written with
- This port, and the complete source of this bundle: @SOURCE_URL@
  Build it with `scripts/build-aymidi.sh`, which fetches every dependency below at the commit named here.

## License

The bundle as a whole is licensed under the **GNU General Public License, version 2** (`LICENSE`).

AyMidi is under the GNU General Public License, version 2 (`licenses/AyMidi-GPL-2.0.txt`). It contains [Ayumi](https://github.com/true-grue/ayumi) by Peter Sovietov (MIT, see the text below); DPF is ISC (`licenses/DPF-ISC.txt`). Both are compatible with the GPL; `module.wasm` as a whole is distributed under the GPL-2.0.

This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied
warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the licenses for details.

The bundle holds the DSP only (`module.wasm`): DPF's own CLAP wrapper compiled to WebAssembly. The plugin's graphical
editor is not part of it, hosts show the plugin's parameters instead.

